# What NOT to upload to Vercel.  (S-08)
#
# Before this, the file listed only `_cms/`, so the whole build toolchain and the
# institution docs were publicly downloadable from production: /preflight.py,
# /_gen_csp_hashes.py, /docs/DECISIONS.md and /REVIEW_WORKORDER_2026-07.md all
# returned 200. The harm is not a credential leak — secrets come from env vars —
# it is that DECISIONS.md and BACKLOG.md enumerate known-unfixed weaknesses, so
# the site published its own weak-point list, alongside the admin endpoint layout
# and the CSP generation logic.
#
# VERIFIED BEFORE EXCLUDING ANY OF THIS (S-08 required proving nothing here is
# read at request time):
#   * there are NO Python serverless functions — api/ is entirely .js, so
#     dropping *.py cannot remove a route;
#   * neither api/ nor middleware.js touches the filesystem (no fs import, no
#     readFileSync, no __dirname) — they fetch content over the GitHub API;
#   * every tracked .py lives at the repo root and no HTML references one;
#   * no page links to /docs/ or to any .md;
#   * the generator chain and the checkers run in CI and locally from the git
#     checkout, which .vercelignore does not affect.
#
# MUST STAY DEPLOYED: _check_deploy_exposure.py derives this from `git ls-files`
# rather than a hand list, so a newly tracked API route or asset is protected
# automatically. It covers assets/ blog/ en/ admin/ tools/ pagefind/ api/ plus
# the root runtime files (vercel.json — the routing config itself — middleware.js,
# sw.js, manifest.json, package.json for @vercel/og, robots/sitemap/llms/
# opensearch, icons and images). The pattern SET is pinned there too, so an
# over-broad exclusion cannot be added without a deliberate edit to the checker.

# Pre-existing: CMS working area
_cms/

# Local-only artefacts (untracked, but keep CLI deploys clean too)
__pycache__/
node_modules/
hs_expected_min_j86c9_ek/

# Build + review toolchain. Runs in CI and locally, never at request time.
*.py

# Repository documentation and process files. docs/DECISIONS.md and
# docs/BACKLOG.md in particular list unfixed weaknesses.
docs/
*.md

# CI configuration, git hooks and browser tests
.github/
.githooks/
scripts/
tests/
playwright.config.js
playwright.seo.config.js

# Deployment procedure — runtime-unreferenced, and it documents how releases
# and any overwrite bypass are performed.
deploy.ps1
deploy.bat
